LAST-MODIFIED:20260809T163925Z
SEQUENCE:1786293565
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260810
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260811
SUMMARY:Full-Body Athletic Strength
DESCRIPTION:Overview:\nMacros: 3500 kcal\, 180 g protein\, 505 g carbs\, 1
 00 g fat\nMacro timing: hit the higher protein target with 40-45 g protei
 n in 4 meals\, plus 50-80 g carbs before heavy lifting and carbs again af
 ter.\nCategory: gym\nRun volume: 0 km\n\n\nWarm-Up:\n- 7 min easy cardio\
 , squat-to-stand\, band pull-aparts\, push-ups\, and hinge ramp sets.\n\n
 \nMain Work:\n- Incline press\, shoulder press\, or bench press: top set 
 1 x 6-8 at RPE 8\, then 2-3 back-off sets x 8-10 at RPE 7-8.\n- Trap-bar 
 deadlift or Romanian deadlift: 2-3 x 5-6 at RPE 7-8\, leave 2-3 RIR.\n- P
 ull-ups or chest-supported rows: 4 x 6-10 at RPE 8 paired with front-foot
  elevated split squat or hack squat 3 x 8-10 per leg at RPE 8.\n- Shoulde
 r\, trap\, and quad finisher: lateral raises 2-3 x 15-20\, dumbbell trap 
 raise 2 x 12-15\, leg extension 2 x 12-15\, then weighted sit-ups 2 x 8-1
 2.\n- Activation: light good mornings: 2 x 12-15 at RPE 5-6 using no more
  than 50% of normal working load\; stop if symptoms rise or the next morn
 ing is worse.\n\n\nFueling:\n- Hit daily macros\, keep protein near targe
 t\, and place carbohydrates before and after training.\n\n\nRecovery:\n- 
 Sleep window stays 22:00-06:00\; add mobility if joints feel stiff.\n\n\n
 Progression & Guardrails:\n- Progression: double progression\; add load o
 nly when presses\, hinges\, and pulls are all stable at RPE 8 or lower.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
