SUMMARY:Active Recovery at Home
DESCRIPTION:Overview:\nMacros: 3150 kcal\, 165 g protein\, 385 g carbs\, 1
 05 g fat\nMacro timing: keep protein evenly split across meals and place 
 most carbs around activity.\nCategory: recovery\nRun volume: 0 km\n\n\nAd
 justments:\n- Reduced for prior-month recovery feedback.\n\n\nWarm-Up:\n-
  5-10 min easy movement\, joint prep\, and 2-3 gradual ramp sets before l
 oading.\n\n\nMain Work:\n- Active recovery circuit: 15-20 minutes at RPE 
 3-4\; feel better\, not trained.\n- Equipment: yoga mat and elastic band 
 are required and available\; the 12 kg kettlebell is optional and not nee
 ded.\n- Transitions: take no more than 15 seconds between elements.\n- Fi
 rst pass: complete every listed element once\; never omit an element from
  the first pass.\n- Cat-cow: 6-8 repetitions.\n- Open-book rotations: 6 p
 er side.\n- 90/90 hip switches: 8 per side.\n- Push-ups: 8-12 repetitions
 \, stopping at least four reps before failure.\n- Band pull-aparts or fac
 e pulls: 15-20 repetitions.\n- Banded hip-flexor marches: 8 per side.\n- 
 Banded flutter kicks: 15-20 seconds.\n- Glute bridges: 12 repetitions.\n-
  Calf and ankle mobility: 60 seconds per side.\n- Repeat from the top onl
 y until at least 15 minutes\; truncate only the second pass as needed and
  stop at 20 minutes.\n\n\nFueling:\n- Hit daily macros\, keep protein nea
 r target\, and place carbohydrates before and after training.\n\n\nRecove
 ry:\n- Sleep window stays 22:00-06:00\; add mobility if joints feel stiff
 .
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
